From 3cbd2077a95ae3c905fbb13519bb3a2ca96dd7fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 19:47:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 0814/3799] soh: rename func_80078E18 ->
 HealthMeter_SetHealthToDisplayed

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: assigns the interface's animated health value back onto gSaveContext.health. Unused (no callers), but the single statement leaves no ambiguity about what it does.
Defined in soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c b/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c
index cd6de967e..9d28860ea 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_lifemeter.c
@@ -285,7 +285,8 @@ void HealthMeter_Update(PlayState* play) {
     sBeatingHeartsDDEnv[2] = (u8)(bFactor + ddColor.b) & 0xFF;
 }
 
-s32 func_80078E18(PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80078E18: assigns the interface's animated health value back onto gSaveContext.health. Unused (no callers), but the single statement leaves no ambiguity about what it does.
+s32 HealthMeter_SetHealthToDisplayed(PlayState* play) {
     gSaveContext.health = play->interfaceCtx.unk_226;
     return 1;
 }
